$bog_vmap_app $mol_view
	doc_src \
	- CSS of the document, and only of the document: this is what an export carries.
	- Canvas placement of free parts rides `spots` instead and never joins this, so
	- the export cannot pick up a world coordinate even by accident.
	doc_css \
	spots? *
	- Property name of the node picked on the canvas, `null` when nothing is picked.
	- The primary of `picked` below: the one the inspector is open on. Read this to
	- follow a single selection, and `picked` where a whole set matters.
	selected? null
	- Every node picked on the canvas, in the order they were taken. A band swept
	- over the canvas writes here, and a carry and a delete read it.
	picked? /string
	doc_js *
	doc_root \
	- The sandbox is a sibling module with no page of its own, so what is derived
	- from the address of THIS page is the address of its bundle, which the markup
	- of the frame names. The dev server and a deploy both work with nothing
	- configured. There is exactly one page in the project and this is it.
	scene_bundle \
	- The palette field: links separated by commas, stored exactly as typed. The
	- first http(s) one is the donor pack, the rest are lands of Giper Baza. One
	- value for the whole editor: the palette offers what the scene has actually
	- loaded, and the two must never drift apart. Derived from it: `pack_link` for
	- the pack the frame is keyed by, `lands` for the library, `libs` for the scene.
	- Empty is the standard palette: the `part` module of this very pack.
	links? \
	palette_showed? true
	inspect_showed? true
	code_showed? false
	- The three texts of the class the code panel has in scope, two way, plus the
	- switch that chooses the scope: one node of a class, or a whole class.
	code_whole? false
	code_source? \
	code_js? \
	code_css? \
	- Handwritten body and styles of the ROOT class, two way. The code panel writes
	- into the class it has in scope, which is this one whenever the picked node is
	- not declared with a class of the document; `doc_js`/`doc_css` carry the bodies
	- of every class to the scene beside the text.
	root_js? \
	root_css? \
	- Persistence: the documents of the user in Giper Baza. One for the whole
	- editor, handed to the switcher in the head bar; text and placement read
	- through it and write back into it.
	store $bog_vmap_app_store
	sub <= body /$mol_view
	-
	Head $mol_bar
		sub /
			<= Brand $mol_view
				sub /
					\vmap
			<= Palette_check $mol_check
				title \Полка
				checked? <=> palette_showed?
			<= Inspect_check $mol_check
				title \Свойства
				checked? <=> inspect_showed?
			<= Code_check $mol_check
				title \Код
				hint \Три текста выбранного узла: view.tree, JS и CSS
				checked? <=> code_showed?
			<= Zoom_out $mol_button_minor
				title \−
				hint \Отдалить
				click? <=> zoom_out? null
			<= Zoom_title $mol_view
				sub /
					<= zoom_title \
			<= Zoom_in $mol_button_minor
				title \+
				hint \Приблизить
				click? <=> zoom_in? null
			<= Reset $mol_button_minor
				title \Сбросить вид
				click? <=> camera_reset? null
			- A page of the document: a node with a `sub` of its own, laid out by
			- tree inside. Nothing marks it as an artboard — the `sub` is the whole
			- difference, see section 8 of the architecture.
			<= Board $mol_button_minor
				title \Артборд
				hint \Положить страницу: прямоугольник ширины макета, вёрстка внутри по дереву
				click? <=> board_add? null
			<= Delete $mol_button_minor
				title \Удалить
				hint <= delete_hint \
				enabled <= selection_showed false
				click? <=> node_delete? null
			- Publishing the picked part into the library of the user, link included.
			- The declaration goes in as the inspector reads it, and the part name as
			- the picked property; the store of libraries is the button's own.
			<= Publish $bog_vmap_app_publish
				part <= publish_part \
				source <= node_source? \
				- Method and rule of the picked part, cut out of the two texts of the
				- class the code editor writes. Without these a published component
				- would arrive at the next document with its behaviour left behind.
				js <= node_js \
				css <= node_css \
				doc <= doc_src
				classes / <= doc_root
			- Name of the root class, editable, right beside the button that spells
			- out the folder it chooses. The folder of an export follows from the
			- class names — section 10 — so this field and that title are two halves
			- of one decision and stand together.
			-
			- Committed on Enter and on leaving the field, NEVER on a keystroke, the
			- same as the name of a node in the inspector: a rename rewrites the
			- document and remakes the node that holds the class, so writing per
			- letter would rename the class to every prefix of what is being typed.
			<= Root_name $mol_string
				hint \Имя корневого класса
				value? <=> root_draft? \
				submit? <=> root_submit? null
				event *
					^
					blur? <=> root_submit? null
			- Sources of the document, as one archive of a real MAM module. The whole
			- promise of the tool ends here, so the folder the module must go to is
			- written in the title itself and not only in the hint: section 10 says
			- the folder is not free, and the author has to see the one their class
			- names chose.
			<= Download $mol_button_download
				title <= export_title \
				hint <= export_hint \
				enabled <= export_ready false
				blob <= export_blob $mol_blob
				file_name <= export_file \
			<= Status $mol_view
				sub /
					<= status \
	-
	Alarm $mol_view
		sub /
			<= error \
	-
	- Why the document does not export, in the very sentences the code panel says
	- about the same mistake: both ask the export for its complaints, so there is
	- one way of speaking about it and not two.
	-
	- On the strip and not in the panel alone, although the panel is where the code
	- is written: the panel is folded by default and shows the picked node, while a
	- refusal comes from the whole document and can name a class nobody has open.
	- A person who pressed a dead button has to read the reason without hunting.
	Export_note $mol_view
		sub <= export_rows /$mol_view
	Export_row* $mol_view
		sub / <= export_text* \
	-
	- Why the root class was not renamed. On the strip beside the refusal of the
	- export, because it is about the document as a whole; a `$mol_string` that
	- throws out of its setter puts the message into `setCustomValidity`, which on
	- a page without a form is nowhere at all.
	Root_note $mol_view
		sub / <= root_title_note \
	-
	- The scene has stopped answering. Its own strip and not the error one: an
	- error means the scene spoke, this means it did not, and the only thing that
	- helps is on this strip.
	Stall $mol_view
		sub /
			<= Stall_note $mol_view sub / <= stall_note \
			<= Stall_reload $mol_button_minor
				title \Перезагрузить сцену
				hint \Поднять кадр заново. Документ хранится в редакторе и не потеряется
				click? <=> scene_restart? null
	-
	- Panel beside the canvas, canvas taking whatever is left.
	Body $mol_view
		sub <= body_main /$mol_view
	-
	- The left edge of the editor: which document is open, and what can be put into
	- it. The two belong together — both answer «what am I working on» — and both
	- are lists, so the head bar is left to the tools that act on the open document.
	Side $mol_view
		sub /
			<= Scenes $bog_vmap_app_scenes
				store <= store
			<= Shelf $bog_vmap_app_shelf
				links? <=> links?
				- The address the host derived, not the one the panel would derive
				- from the field on its own: an empty field means the pack of this
				- very deploy, and only the host knows where that is.
				pack_link <= pack_link
				land_classes <= lib_classes /$mol_tree2
				- Names of the classes the library holds, for the objects of the
				- connected application. A binding and not a read of our own: the
				- fetch behind it must happen inside the panel, where a dead address
				- shows up on the one list it belongs to.
				class_list <= lib_class_list /string
				- An item asked for by a click rather than by a drag. The shelf says
				- which one; where it goes is the canvas's answer.
				place? <=> shelf_place? \
	-
	- Properties of the picked node, on the far edge from the palette: one panel
	- offers what can be added, the other what the added thing can do, and the canvas
	- keeps the middle. Either can be folded away when the canvas needs the room.
	Aside $mol_view
		sub <= aside_content /$mol_view
	-
	- The inspector reads ONE class, and a part declared on the canvas is exactly
	- that: `Button_minor $mol_button_minor` is a class named `Button_minor` with
	- `$mol_button_minor` for a base, so its own lines are its own ports and the rest
	- come down the chain. Nothing had to be added to the inspector to fit.
	- The classes of the attached lands ride in through `peers` beside the root of
	- the document: the inspector already resolves a peer's ports through the same
	- index as the pack's, so a land class needs nothing added on its side.
	Inspect $bog_vmap_app_inspect
		source? <=> node_source? \
		peers <= node_peers /$mol_tree2
		pack <= pack_link \
		- The name field renames through the editor and not through the class the
		- inspector holds: the name of a node is also the key of the pick, of the
		- placement and of every reference in the document, and only the editor knows
		- all four. The refusal comes back the same way, in words.
		class_title? <=> node_title? \
		title_note <= node_title_note \
	-
	- What stands in the panel while nothing is picked. A state, not a blank: the
	- inspector handed an empty source would fail to find a class in it and show an
	- error where an invitation belongs.
	Idle $mol_view
		sub /
			<= idle_note \Выберите узел на холсте, чтобы править его свойства
	-
	- Three sources of the picked node, next to the inspector: one panel says what
	- the node can do, the other says how it does it. Folded away by its own check
	- in the head bar, like the two panels beside it.
	-
	- `node_source` is the very binding the inspector edits, so a change made with
	- the mouse shows up in the text with no path of its own; the three texts of the
	- class are those of the class in scope, sliced by the panel.
	-
	- The scope is the editor's and not the panel's: which class the three texts
	- belong to depends on whether the picked node is declared with a class the
	- document itself authors, and only the owner of the document knows that. That
	- is also how the body and the styles of a second class are reached at all.
	Code $bog_vmap_app_code
		klass <= code_klass \
		prop <= code_prop \
		hooks <= code_hooks /string
		whole? <=> code_whole?
		source? <=> code_source?
		node_source? <=> node_source?
		js? <=> code_js?
		css? <=> code_css?
		error <= code_error \
	-
	- Component library of the host: the pack, with the lands of the field stacked
	- on it. `script_link()` is the bundle the scene is told to load; `land_trees()` feed the
	- palette and the inspector; `parts()` go to the scene. The pack tree itself is
	- fetched by the palette from the same address, the two share one `$mol_fetch`
	- cell. The only object in the editor that opens a land of the field.
	Lib $bog_vmap_lib_land_stack
		pack <= pack_link
		lands <= lands /string
	-
	- What the pointer is carrying, drawn at the pointer. Rendered only while a drag
	- is on, so it costs nothing the rest of the time.
	Ghost $mol_view
		style *
			left <= ghost_left \0px
			top <= ghost_top \0px
		sub /
			<= ghost_title \
	-
	Pane $bog_vmap_app_pane
		scene_bundle <= scene_bundle
		pack_uri <= pack_script \
		doc_src <= doc_src
		doc_css <= doc_css
		spots? <=> spots?
		picked? <=> picked?
		doc_js <= doc_js
		doc_root <= doc_root
		libs <= libs /$bog_vmap_bridge_part
		carrying <= carrying false
		- Wires: the pane draws them from the document and its ports, and writes a
		- new or a dropped one back through these two events, never into the text.
		wires <= doc_wires /$bog_vmap_lang_link
		part_ports* <= part_ports* /$bog_vmap_app_wire_port
		link_add? <=> link_add? null
		link_drop? <=> link_drop? null
		- Nodes that carry a `sub` of their own, so the pane knows where a drop goes
		- into the tree instead of onto the canvas, and where to draw the line.
		containers <= doc_containers /string
		doc_names <= doc_names /string
		axis* <= doc_axis* \
		tree_move? <=> tree_move? null
